  <!-- Introduction -->
  <Container first>
    <h1>Introduction</h1>
    <p class="text">
      An LLM agent that calls tools sends sessions of many turns to its serving engine: each prompt is the
      previous context plus the output of the tool just run. Serving engines such as SGLang and vLLM
      keep the previous turn's KV in a prefix cache, so a follow-up turn whose prefix is still cached
      prefills only its new tokens. In our workload a hit prefills 551 tokens and a miss about 11,100;
      per session, prefill work with every turn missing is about 16 times that with every follow-up
      hitting.
    </p>
  </Container>

