  <Container>
    <h2>A Renewal Recursion along FIFO Orbits</h2>
    <p class="text">
      Model F is a fluid FIFO server on which every turn misses. Turn <Tex src="k" /> costs
      <Tex src={String.raw`c_k>0`} /> GPU seconds when it misses, and <Tex src={String.raw`G_k=P(T\ge k)`} />. The all-miss capacity and the load are
    </p>
    <Tex block src={String.raw`\lambda_{\mathrm{miss}}=\Big(\sum_k c_kG_k\Big)^{-1},\qquad \rho=\lambda/\lambda_{\mathrm{miss}}.`} />
    <p class="text">
      Its assumptions (F1)–(F6): every turn misses; the server works at unit rate while anything is
      pending; service is first come, first served at the request level; a completed turn
      <Tex src={String.raw`k<T`} /> rejoins the tail at once as turn <Tex src="k+1" />; new sessions arrive as
      turn 1 at rate <Tex src={String.raw`\lambda`} />; and the initial pending mass is finite with positive
      work. A request joining at time <Tex src="u" /> completes at <Tex src={String.raw`f(u)=u+V(u)`} />,
      where <Tex src="V(u)" /> is the pending work, so <Tex src="V" /> is also the gap between a session's
      consecutive turns. A FIFO orbit is <Tex src={String.raw`u_{n+1}=f(u_n)`} />, with cycles
      <Tex src={String.raw`\Delta_n=u_{n+1}-u_n`} />.
    </p>
    <p class="text">
      FIFO maps the requests that join during one cycle onto the requests that complete during the next,
      and the turn-<Tex src="k" /> mass joining there is <Tex src={String.raw`\lambda G_k\Delta_{n-k}`} />.
      Lemma 1 turns this into a linear recursion for the cycles,
    </p>
    <Tex block src={String.raw`\Delta_n=\sum_{k=1}^{\min(n,K)}\lambda c_kG_k\,\Delta_{n-k}+h_n,`} />
    <p class="text">
      with <Tex src={String.raw`h_n\ge 0`} />, <Tex src={String.raw`h_n=0`} /> for <Tex src={String.raw`n\ge K`} />,
      and <Tex src={String.raw`\sum_n h_n=V_{\mathrm{tot}}(u_0)`} />, where <Tex src={String.raw`V_{\mathrm{tot}}`} />
      is the remaining all-miss work of every session present, which changes at rate
      <Tex src={String.raw`\rho-1`} /> while the server is busy. Its growth rate is a Perron root:
    </p>
    <Tex block src={String.raw`\lambda\sum_k c_kG_kz^{-k}=1,\qquad z>1\iff\rho>1.`} />
    <h2>Where Every Trapped State Goes</h2>
    <p class="text">
      Theorem 1(a): every trapped state converges to a known self-similar regime, in which
    </p>
    <Tex block src={String.raw`\frac{V(t)}{t}\to\gamma=z-1,\qquad \frac{N(t)}{t}\to\alpha=\lambda\big(1-E[z^{-T}]\big),\qquad D=\lambda E[z^{-T}],\qquad \nu^z_k=\frac{G_kz^{-k}}{\sum_jG_jz^{-j}}.`} />
    <p class="text">
      The gap between a session's turns grows linearly at rate <Tex src={String.raw`\gamma`} />, the number
      of sessions present <Tex src="N" /> grows at <Tex src={String.raw`\alpha`} />, sessions complete at
      rate <Tex src="D" />, and the turns served follow the tilted mix <Tex src={String.raw`\nu^z`} />
      rather than the stationary mix <Tex src={String.raw`\nu_k\propto G_k`} />: the turns served are young
      and short. Proposition 1(a), classical in substance, covers the other side: the queue empties if
      and only if <Tex src={String.raw`\rho<1`} />, at <Tex src={String.raw`V_{\mathrm{tot}}(0)/(1-\rho)`} />,
      and at <Tex src={String.raw`V_{\mathrm{tot}}(0)`} /> with arrivals stopped. Near threshold,
      Proposition 1(c) gives <Tex src={String.raw`\gamma=(\rho-1)/\bar k_c+O((\rho-1)^2)`} /> and
      <Tex src={String.raw`\alpha/(\lambda-\lambda_{\mathrm{miss}})\to E[T]/\bar k_c`} />, where
      <Tex src={String.raw`\bar k_c=\sum_k k\,c_kG_k\big/\sum_k c_kG_k`} />.
    </p>
  </Container>

