  <Container>
    <p class="text">
      Once formed, the trap held. Over 50 trapped runs before the blind tests, about 100 trapped hours, no
      300 s window after the trap formed reached a follow-up hit fraction of 0.5; the highest was 0.16
      (a post hoc summary). The registered dose response places the basin boundary between bursts of 40
      and 60 sessions in every seed, with a burst of 50 trapping 1 of 3. Not every registered rule was
      met: lengthening every tool call that starts in <Tex src={String.raw`[1200,2100)`} /> s by 30 s
      trapped 1 of 3 runs, so that rule (traps in 2 of 3) failed, and at the tenth rate, Llama-3.1-8B at
      the lower rate, the trap rule failed on its backlog-growth condition.
    </p>
  </Container>

  <Container>
    <h2>The Theory against 57 Stuck Runs</h2>
    <p class="text">
      We derived the theory after the stuck runs were read, so this comparison is retrospective. No
      parameter is fitted to any trap measurement, and model F's capacity is within 4% of the all-miss
      capacity measured on the engine with prefix caching disabled and 32 sessions kept running. Across
      the 57 stuck runs:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><p class="text">
        the mean served prompt is within 3% of model F's in 50 of the 57 runs: the trapped engine serves
        turns 9–41% shorter than the stationary mix;
      </p></li>
      <li><p class="text">
        gap growth, measured over predicted, has median 1.01 (mean 0.96); per run it ranges from 0.04 to
        1.81;
      </p></li>
      <li><p class="text">
        every stuck run completes sessions above <Tex src={T.lref} />, at 1.10–2.03 <Tex src={T.lref} />
        (up to 2.40 in the from-empty runs), and net of the congested engine's faster token rate,
        completions still exceed <Tex src={T.lref} /> by a factor of 1.08–1.81 in every one of the 57;
      </p></li>
      <li><p class="text">
        the backlog slope, over model F's <Tex src={String.raw`\alpha`} />, has mean 0.99 and median 1.06,
        where the quasi-static reading gives 1.36–1.59.
      </p></li>
    </ul>
  </Container>

