      {f.mult}× the measured all-miss rate, plus a burst of {f.burstN} at {fmt(f.tB)} s. The top engine
      is left alone and stays at zero hits to the end. The bottom one gets the paper's rescue cap of
      {f.cap} sessions at {fmt(f.engage)} s: its hits come back by {fmt(f.hitsBack)} s, drop out again
      while the gate drains the backlog, and hold from {fmt(f.hitsHold)} s; the cap comes off at
      {fmt(f.release)} s and the engine stays good. Over the last 3,000 s the trapped engine's turns
      average {fmt(f.trapped.meanPrompt)} prompt tokens, against {fmt(f.model.Pz)} in model F and
      {fmt(f.model.Pstat)} in the normal turn mix. The site's checks run the same code against the
      paper's Python engine and get identical counts.
    </p>
  </Container>

  <Container>
    <p class="text">
      The run was chosen from {f.selection.candidates} seeds as one in which every burst session
      finishes before the end, the cap comes off inside the paper's engine range, and the completion
      rate is closest to model F's. Over {f.further.seeds} further seeds that played no part in the
      choice, {allStuck ? 'every' : `${f.further.stuck} of ${f.further.seeds}`} engine{allStuck ? '' : 's'} that
      get{allStuck ? 's' : ''} the burst and no cap {allStuck ? 'is' : 'are'} stuck at zero hits, the
      trapped engines' served prompts average {f.further.promptOverPz.toFixed(2)} times model F's, and
      their completion rates average {f.further.completionsOverMiss.toFixed(2)} times the all-miss
      capacity, from {f.further.completionsMin.toFixed(2)} to {f.further.completionsMax.toFixed(2)}.
    </p>
